{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "label": "Rolling deployment migration", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Deploy a schema-breaking or key-rotating change without downtime and without coordinated stops; the pattern composes four shipped features into a four-phase deploy and applies identically across journals.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_four_phase_deploy", "label": "The four-phase deploy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Code-first, observation, writer flip, optional cleanup. The cluster as a whole moves forward only when every instance is at the same phase or later.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_migrationchain", "label": "MigrationChain", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Defines every version with the upcaster between them, so a reader handles all registered versions; a reader lacking the newest step throws on the first event it cannot make sense of.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_write_version_pin", "label": "Pinning writeVersion during phase 1", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Readers handle every registered version but writers emit a chosen one; holding writes at the old version until every reader can handle the new one avoids a v1-only instance reading a v2 event it has no upcaster for.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_observation_phase", "label": "Phase 2 observation checkpoint", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A deployment-completion checkpoint, not a deployment step. A fifteen second pipeline can still leave a single instance behind during a network blip, and phase 3 makes that instance non-functional.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_writer_flip", "label": "Phase 3 writer flip and its rollback cost", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Rollback stops being trivial here: any new-shape event since the flip cannot be read by an old reader. Forward-fixing with another chain entry is always preferable to restoring from a pre-flip snapshot.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_backfill_cleanup", "label": "Phase 4 optional backfill", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Optional because the upcast cost is typically nanoseconds per event; many systems live indefinitely with mixed-version journals. Run it only when the historical step becomes operational drag.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_migratebetweenjournals", "label": "migrateBetweenJournals", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "For SQL and Cassandra journals with no in-place rewrite, read from the old backend and write an enveloped copy to the new one. Sequence numbers survive, compacted sources included, so snapshot and projection cursors keep their numbering; run the journal copy before the snapshot copy.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_masterkeyring_parallel_story", "label": "Key rotation on the same four-phase shape", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "New bodies stamp the new keyVersion in their manifest while existing bodies still decrypt via the retired entry; a reader missing the retired entry cannot decrypt the historical blobs.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_reencryptprogressstore", "label": "ReEncryptProgressStore durable resume", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Without it a crash forces the resumed run to re-list and re-GET every key from the start - a 24 hour wasted re-walk on a 24 hour sweep. Saving every 500 rewrites means a crash redoes at most 500 objects, a 0.005 percent rewind on a 10M bucket.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_completeness_check_tradeoff", "label": "Disabling the completeness check", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Without it a sweep aborts mid-corpus on the first body referencing a missing version, leaving half the corpus under each key; disabling without an independent audit trades a deterministic pre-flight failure for a mid-corpus abort.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_four_phase_deploy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_migrationchain", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_write_version_pin", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_observation_phase", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_writer_flip", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_backfill_cleanup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_migratebetweenjournals", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_masterkeyring_parallel_story", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_reencryptprogressstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/upgrades/rolling-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_rolling_deployment_migration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_upgrades_rolling_migration_comple